e oven the cookie  dough is ready and it can be decorated  with nuts or covered with chocolate what  is this called Clinton Clinton okay it's  nice I think it's got some nuts in it  and I thought it's a chocolate but it's  a mix of a chocolate and something else  it's nice we have the similar Japanese  sweet like this one and softwa and the  hard one and cinnamon flavor so we like  it no my style it's like to Christmas  taste  if you want to escape the Christmas  hustle and bustle you can visit Aachen  Cathedral most tourists want to  experience something of the city's long  history as well as the Christmas market  they found it really cute here this cozy  old town and they liked the fact that  there is no trashy stuff and none of the  bustle of the Christmas Fair the shops  in the winding narrow streets are also  in the Christmas mood most printin are  sold at this time of year but they're  available all year round there's even a  statue featuring the gingerbread  specialty in front of fund and dollar  one of Atkins oldest cafes inside the  walls are decorated with wooden biscuit  molds they were used to shape a  forerunner of today's printin which  arrived in Aachen from neighboring  Belgium in the 16th century and then  developed from there the cookies are  named after the English word to print  the mould is stamped into the dough  as darkness falls it starts feeling more  and more Christmassy the market begins  to fill up and even if you're not  feeling like having anything sweet you  can't go for a day in Aachen without  seeing gingerbread cookies somewhere
 

